# Runbook: {{ name }}

Owner: {{ owner }} ({{ function }}). Built with the deployment kit; spec in `config/usecases/{{ id }}.yaml`.

## When something looks wrong
- Proposals edited or rejected more than the alert in the spec: open the desk's use case page, read
  the last rejected proposals and their review reasons, and add the failing cases to the dev set.
- Gateway errors or budget refusals: cases fall back to people automatically; check `/v1/gateway` calls.
- Wrong action executed: every executed action has an approval id; reverse it in the source system
  and record the case.

## Switching it off
Remove the countries from the rollout waves in the spec; nothing else needs to change.
